Consider one transverse coordinate of an open string and subtract its center of mass. The oscillator expansion used here is schematic: $X(\sigma)-X_{\mathrm{cm}}
  \sim
  \sum_{n=1}^{\infty}
  \frac{a_n+a_n^\dagger}{\sqrt n}\cos(n\sigma).$ The essential ingredients are the cosine modes, the oscillator operators, and the factor $1/\sqrt n$. Exact normalizations play no role in the size argument.  (Editorial clarification: The precise expansion contains convention-dependent factors of $\alpha'$, numerical constants, and a choice of oscillator notation. Equation [eq:l09-mode-expansion] retains only the dependence needed for the ultraviolet estimate, just as in the board derivation.)

